Fixes from upstream lutinglt/gitea-github-theme (main @ 356b195, 2026-11-24)
that whereareiam/forgejo-github-theme 1.6.0 does not have yet. The fork split
off at upstream 1.27.0 (7c20142) and has since rewritten most pages for
Forgejo's markup, so these are ported by hand, not cherry-picked. Upstream
commits that target Gitea-only markup (Actions list, branch tabs, org RSS
button, Gitea 1.25 adaptation) are left out: the fork has its own templates
for those pages.

  990ce72  pink: restore the primary button colour; dropdown menus above the diff box
  44ba08e  pink: background and border contrast like GitHub
  827d664  catppuccin: text, label and underline colours closer to GitHub
  04468aa  snappier overlay animation (120ms, 6px); no slide-in per branch or log step;
           PR branch label padding
  7188497  tooltips placed above slide up; PR popup opens in 80ms
  d3f5fbe
  a94c604  high-contrast: outline on the repo name on hover
  279db3c  small and tiny buttons 28px; settings header button padding
  cc9eb94  admin settings buttons use the normal padding; code copy button 28x28
  6be4719  pagination: background on hover instead of a border
  0fe8140  the active-tab underline does not catch clicks

Applied with `patch -p1 -F0` in ../Dockerfile, so any hunk that no longer
matches fails the build instead of landing in the wrong place.
